    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NNKdpkG3GKrYB8hHbRYuGq)_\n\n## What\n\n- New page `docs/architecture/tabspaces-workspaces.org`: how workspaces are made in `sp-tabs`, `sp-workspaces` and `sp-dashboard`.\n- Table of the existing workspaces: command, key, tab name, what opens.\n- How Home and the Dashboard relate, and how the Dashboard reaches workspaces (`sp-dashboard--workspace-dispatch`).\n- Step-by-step guide to add a workspace, with a template and the Dashboard hookup.\n- Known rough edges found while reading, and a manual test checklist for a new workspace.\n- `sp-tabs.org` fixed: it still said buffer lists are filtered by default (stale after #465).\n- Pointers to the new page from `sp-tabs.org`, `sp-workspaces.org` and `sp-dashboard.org`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Documentation only: no `.el` change, no tangled block touched, no CHANGELOG edit.\n- Read from the code, not run in a GUI: the claim that `sp--workspace-setup` runs before the Dashboard exists (so its Dashboard branch is probably a no-op).\n- Digits 6 to 9 are described as unused \"as far as the config shows\".\n- Not done: a registry macro that would define command, key and Dashboard wrapper from one entry (mentioned as an option).\n\n## Manual testing checklist\n\n- [ ] The new page renders in Org and its links to the module docs resolve.\n- [ ] The links added to `sp-tabs.org`, `sp-workspaces.org` and `sp-dashboard.org` open the new page.\n- [ ] The workspace table matches your real keys (leader 1 to 5, `C-x p N`).\n- [ ] Follow the guide once with a throwaway workspace and check that it works as written.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD9ebSHChd2mUbx219)_",
